      "cooked": "<p>Hello everyone. My first time here.</p>\n<p>I've been creating loads of heroes to feel the game and I have so much to say about this system, but I'll start with something very simple: something I actually sense as an actual error. So Form-Changer gives you an obligatory Ability:</p>\n<p><strong>Change Forms</strong>&nbsp;- perform a basic action using [power] and then switch to an available form.</p>\n<p>Fine. Then there are two optional Abilities to take one from:</p>\n<p><strong>Form Recovery</strong> -&nbsp;Attack using [power], recover Min Die Health and convert back to the base form;</p>\n<p>or</p>\n<p><strong>Surprise Shift</strong> -&nbsp;Attack using [power], lose your Min Die Health and switch to any available form.</p>\n<p>Problem is, <strong>Change Forms</strong>,&nbsp;which is obligatory, does the same as <strong>Surprise Shift</strong>, without any Health loss. For me, either <strong>Change Forms</strong> should be nerfed (maybe \"perform any basic action except Attacks...\" or \"perform a basic action using your Min Die and...\"), or <strong>Suprise Shift</strong> should have some kind of bonus (\"the attack cannot be defended or reacted against\" or \"use your Max die\", for example).</p>\n<p>Or am I missing something??</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Thanks in advance for the reply.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:53:04.659Z",
